---
const rawBase = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const base = rawBase.endsWith("/") ? rawBase : `${rawBase}/`;
const repo = "https://github.com/izzet/quotabubble";
const canonical = new URL(`${base}privacy/`, Astro.site).href;

const services = [
  ["Claude Code", "api.anthropic.com"],
  ["Codex", "chatgpt.com"],
  ["Google Antigravity", "Google Cloud Code endpoints (googleapis.com) and oauth2.googleapis.com to refresh its token"],
  ["GitHub Copilot", "api.github.com"],
  ["Cursor", "cursor.com"],
  ["OpenCode", "opencode.ai"],
  ["DeepSeek", "api.deepseek.com"],
  ["OpenRouter", "openrouter.ai"],
  ["Kimi Code", "the Kimi Code API host configured by your Kimi Code CLI"],
  ["Z.ai", "api.z.ai"],
  ["Grok", "cli-chat-proxy.grok.com"],
  ["Zed", "cloud.zed.dev"],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy policy — QuotaBubble</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="QuotaBubble privacy policy: it runs on your device, reads the logins your AI tools already store, and sends nothing to its developer."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href={`${base}favicon.png`} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0e0e11" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <p class="back"><a href={base}>← QuotaBubble</a></p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="dim">Last updated: September 2026</p>

      <p>
        QuotaBubble is a desktop widget that shows how much of your AI coding tools' usage limits you have
        left. It runs entirely on your device. There is no QuotaBubble account, server, analytics, or
        telemetry, and <strong>the developer receives none of your data</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>What QuotaBubble accesses on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Logins your AI tools already store.</strong> To ask each service for your usage, QuotaBubble
          reads the sign-in token that the tool keeps in your user profile (for example a file in your home
          folder) or in the operating system's credential store (Windows Credential Manager). It reads only
          the tools that are detected or that you enable in Settings, and it never modifies, copies, or
          exports those files.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>API keys you enter.</strong> For services that use an API key, you can type one into
          Settings. It is saved in your operating system's credential store. If none is available, it is
          saved in QuotaBubble's local settings file instead, and Settings tells you when that happens.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What QuotaBubble sends, and to whom</h2>
      <p>
        QuotaBubble makes requests only to the service each login belongs to, to read your own usage and
        quota numbers. The login token is sent to that service as authentication, over HTTPS, and nowhere
        else. Nothing is sent to the developer or to any other third party.
      </p>
      <ul class="hosts">
        {services.map(([name, host]) => (
          <li><strong>{name}</strong> — {host}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Those services handle your data under their own privacy policies. QuotaBubble contacts a service
        only if you use it and it is enabled.
      </p>

      <h2>What QuotaBubble stores on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Everything below lives in a QuotaBubble folder in your user profile
        (<code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\quotabubble</code> on Windows) and is not uploaded anywhere.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your settings (which services are enabled, appearance, notification thresholds).</li>
        <li>The last successful usage numbers, so the widget can keep showing them during a network error.</li>
        <li>
          A log file for troubleshooting. Tokens, keys, cookies, and email addresses are redacted before
          anything is written.
        </li>
        <li>
          An optional usage history, <strong>off by default</strong>. It is only collected if you turn it on
          in Settings.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Disable any service in Settings, and QuotaBubble stops reading its login and contacting it.</li>
        <li>Clear an API key in Settings to remove it from the credential store.</li>
        <li>Delete the QuotaBubble folder above to remove all local data, or uninstall the app.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>QuotaBubble is a developer tool and is not directed at children. It collects no personal information.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be published on this page with a new date. The
        full source code is public at <a href={repo}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble</a>, so you can verify
        what the app does.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or concerns can be raised as an issue at
        <a href={`${repo}/issues`}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble/issues</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <span>MIT licensed</span>
      <span>·</span>
      <a href={repo}>github.com/izzet/quotabubble</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0e0e11;
    --panel: #16161a;
    --line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    --text: #ececf1;
    --dim: #9a9aa5;
    --accent: #5ec584;
  }
  * {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial,
      sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  main {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 24px 24px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 32px 0 8px;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  code {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  li {
    margin: 6px 0;
  }
  .dim {
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .back {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .hosts {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .hosts strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  footer {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 24px;
    color: var(--dim);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
